IMDb normally uses IMDb's GraphQL service. If that service rejects or fails a
request, the optional TMDB fallback can search for films and TV series and show
their details, cast, poster and first page of reviews.

To enable it, obtain an API Read Access Token from your own TMDB account at
https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api, then enable "Use TMDB when IMDb is
unavailable" and enter the token in IMDb Setup. The token is masked on screen
but stored in the receiver's Enigma2 settings; do not share that settings file.
Search terms and IMDb identifiers are sent to TMDB when the fallback is used.
The source and rating are labelled TMDB: these ratings are not IMDb ratings.
TMDB searches do not include individual episodes. Some IMDb-specific details
are not available from TMDB. Local saving is disabled for TMDB results.

The TMDB credits screen is available from the plugin menu when the fallback is
enabled. TMDB API use is subject to its terms, including attribution and
non-commercial-use requirements: https://www.themoviedb.org/api-terms-of-use
The included tmdb-logo.svg is the approved TMDB logo from
https://www.themoviedb.org/about/logos-attribution. Its gradient is specified
on the path instead of through a CSS class for the Enigma2 SVG renderer.
